Please validate and correct the Armor Class calculation for this character:

```json
{
  "name": "Scout Kira",
  "armorClass": 15,
  "class": "Rogue",
  "race": "Wood Elf",
  "abilities": {
    "dexterity": 18,
    "constitution": 12,
    "wisdom": 14
  },
  "proficiencies": {
    "armor": [
      "Light"
    ]
  },
  "equipment": [
    {
      "item_name": "Studded Leather Armor",
      "item_type": "armor",
      "equipped": true,
      "description": "A suit of studded leather armor worn for protection.",
      "ac_base": 12,
      "ac_bonus": 0,
      "dex_limit": null,
      "armor_category": "light",
      "stealth_disadvantage": false
    }
  ],
  "classFeatures": [
    {
      "name": "Sneak Attack",
      "description": "Once per turn, deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature hit with an attack if you have advantage or an ally is within 5 feet.",
      "source": "Rogue"
    },
    {
      "name": "Cunning Action",
      "description": "You can take a bonus action on each of your turns to Dash, Disengage, or Hide.",
      "source": "Rogue"
    }
  ],
  "racialTraits": [
    {
      "name": "Darkvision",
      "description": "Accustomed to twilit forests and the night sky, you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions. You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light.",
      "source": "Wood Elf"
    }
  ]
}
```

Analyze their equipment, abilities, and class features to determine the correct AC according to 5th edition rules. 

Pay special attention to:
1. Equipped armor and shields
2. Dexterity modifier and armor type limitations
3. Fighting style bonuses (especially Defense)
4. Equipment conflicts (multiple armor pieces)

Provide the corrected character data with proper AC calculation.

